-- risk: additive
--
-- #3132 (decided in #3012) -- an assistant proposes the members' everyday
-- rights as a request, and the person confirms in the app.
--
--   write  set_member_permissions_preset  request_matrix_permission, the
--          preset 'members_can_book' of the member-rights step, one
--          permission at a time (manageRoles)
--
-- The preset is the step's own: book a place, see the calendar, write
-- messages, see one's own account -- nothing administrative. The target
-- (mcp_target_set_member_permissions_preset) refuses before anyone is asked
-- what the command would refuse and names each permission that is granted,
-- from no to yes; its revision is that list. When the workspace requires
-- validation of role changes, request_matrix_permission answers 'pending':
-- the operation answers pending_validation with the same list and the
-- assistant never approves anything.

